Official library containing the database for [URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1617-FurnitureCatalogue.html"]FurnitureCatalogue[/URL]. It is required for FurnitureCatalogue to work.

[COLOR=red][SIZE=4]Database updates ship in this library, independently of FurnitureCatalogue releases.[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=6]AddOns that use this Lib[/SIZE][/COLOR]
[LIST]
[*][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1617-FurnitureCatalogue.html"]FurnitureCatalogue[/URL]
[*][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1865-FurnitureShoppingListFurC2.0patch.html"]FurnitureShoppingList (FurC 2.0 patch)[/URL][/LIST]

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=6]References and contributions[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*][URL="https://github.com/wookiefriseur/LFC/blob/main/LibFurnitureCatalogue/Api.lua"]API reference: every function's arguments, return fields and examples[/URL]
[*][URL="https://wookiefriseur.github.io/LFC/"]Browse and contribute through the web interface[/URL]
[*][URL="https://github.com/wookiefriseur/LFC"]Source and issues on GitHub[/URL]
[/LIST]


[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=6]Look up an item in game[/SIZE][/COLOR]

Type one of these commands in chat:

[code]/lfc 203600
/lfc raw 203600
/lfc db[/code]
[LIST]
[*][B]/lfc 203600[/B] shows the Scribing Altar's sources and any crafting materials.
[*][B]/lfc raw 203600[/B] shows the underlying records, useful when checking or reporting data.
[*][B]/lfc db[/B] shows the installed library version, loading state and item count.
[/LIST]
Replace 203600 with another item ID, or insert an item link after the command. The catalogue describes how to obtain an item, it does not report whether your character owns it or has learned its recipe.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=6]Use the API in your AddOn[/SIZE][/COLOR]


Add this line to your AddOn's manifest (.txt or .addon file), so ESO loads the library first:

[code]## DependsOn: LibFurnitureCatalogue[/code]

Then put this in your AddOn's Lua file:

[highlight="lua"]local LFC = LibFurnitureCatalogue.API

LFC.OnReady(function()
  local entry = LFC.GetEntry(203600)
  if not entry then
    d("No catalogue entry found")
    return
  end

  local name = zo_strformat("<<C:1>>", GetItemLinkName(LFC.GetItemLink(entry.id)))
  d(name)
  d("Known ways to obtain it: " .. #LFC.GetSourceDetails(entry.id))
end)[/highlight]

[B]LFC[/B] is a short local name for [B]LibFurnitureCatalogue.API[/B]. [B]OnReady[/B] waits until the catalogue is available, then runs the function you supplied. If it is already ready, the function runs immediately.

The remaining examples assume you named your variable LFC too. Run item queries after IsReady() returns true or inside OnReady.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Choose the information you need[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*][B]Has(id)[/B]: does this lookup return an entry?
[*][B]GetEntry(id)[/B]: one furnishing's ID, source types, update and recipe ID when known.
[*][B]GetSourceDetails(id)[/B]: each recorded way to obtain it, with details such as vendor, location and price.
[*][B]GetIngredients(id)[/B]: ingredient links and quantities, when a recipe can be resolved.
[*][B]GetItemIds()[/B] and [B]GetEntryCount()[/B]: browse or count the catalogue.
[/LIST]

Item queries accept an item ID or link. A furniture recipe lookup resolves to the furnishing it makes. A record is a Lua table containing named fields and a source record describes 1 way to obtain the furnishing. Several offers can have the same source type.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Check a source type[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[highlight="lua"]local entry = LFC.GetEntry(203600)
local sources = LFC.GetSourceTypes()
if entry and entry.sources[sources.PVP] then
  d("This furnishing has a PvP source")
end[/highlight]

[B]entry.sources[/B] is a set: looking up a source ID gives true when it is present. Use the named constants returned by GetSourceTypes instead of copying numeric values from an example.

The supported entry fields are id, sources, version and blueprint. version and blueprint can be absent. A blueprint ID identifies a recipe, not whether the player knows it. GetEntry returns a copy you can edit without breaking anything.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Show vendors, locations and prices[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[highlight="lua"]for _, record in ipairs(LFC.GetSourceDetails(203600)) do
  local source = record.source
  if source.vendor then
    d(zo_strformat("<<C:1>>", GetString(source.vendor)))
  end

  for _, placement in ipairs(source.locations or {}) do
    if placement.location then
      d(zo_strformat("<<C:1>>", GetZoneNameById(placement.location)))
    end
    if placement.place then
      d(zo_strformat("<<C:1>>", GetString(placement.place)))
    end
  end

  if record.cost then
    d(record.cost.amount .. " " .. GetCurrencyName(record.cost.currency, false, false))
  end
end[/highlight]

This prints the available vendor, place and price fields.. The list uses the preferred display order, but it does not mean the first acquisition type is the best source.

Treat source records as read-only: some nested values refer to shared library data. Use ZO_DeepTableCopy(record) if you need an editable copy.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Turn IDs into readable names[/SIZE][/COLOR]

Different IDs need different ESO functions:

[LIST]
[*]vendor, place and event are string IDs: use GetString.
[*]location is a zone ID: use GetZoneNameById.
[*]achievement is an achievement ID: GetAchievementInfo returns its name first.
[*]quest uses GetQuestName, crate uses GetCrownCrateName.
[*]houses contains collectible IDs: use GetCollectibleName for each one.
[*]Item and ingredient links use GetItemLinkName.
[/LIST]

Fields can be nil, meaning no value was provided. For achievement, quest and crate, [B]0[/B] means a requirement or source exists but its ID is unknown. Check for a positive ID before looking it up (0 is truthy, so true is not enough).

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Show crafting materials[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[highlight="lua"]local materials = LFC.GetIngredients(118991) -- recipe: High Elf Stool, Curved
for ingredientLink, quantity in pairs(materials) do
  d(quantity .. "x " .. zo_strformat("<<C:1>>", GetItemLinkName(ingredientLink)))
end
if next(materials) == nil then
  d("No crafting ingredients found")
end[/highlight]


[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Loading and later updates[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[B]IsReady()[/B] only checks; it does not start loading. [B]OnReady[/B] starts loading if necessary. Before readiness, empty or incomplete results do not mean an item is absent.

[B]GetState()[/B] distinguishes uninitialized, building, ready and failed.

For a window that stays open, lifecycle callbacks keep its status current:

[highlight="lua"]local function showStatus()
  if LFC.IsReady() then
    d("Catalogue: " .. LFC.GetEntryCount() .. " items")
  else
    local state, message = LFC.GetState()
    d("Catalogue: " .. state .. " " .. tostring(message or ""))
  end
end

LFC.RegisterCallback(LFC.Events.SCAN_STARTED, showStatus)
LFC.RegisterCallback(LFC.Events.SCAN_COMPLETE, showStatus)
LFC.RegisterCallback(LFC.Events.SCAN_FAILED, showStatus)
LFC.OnReady(showStatus)
showStatus()
[/highlight]

A status refresh may run more than once during startup. RegisterCallback keeps listening. OnReady runs once. To stop listening, call UnregisterCallback with the same event, function and optional argument used to register.

If you cache query results, compare [B]GetDBRevision()[/B] before reusing them. A changed revision means you need fresh results.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Names, constants and versions[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*][B]GetSourceTypes()[/B]: source name to numeric ID, for comparisons.
[*][B]GetSourceTypeInfo()[/B]: source ID to stable key and English description, for exports and logs. These labels are not translated UI text.
[*][B]GetDataVersions()[/B]: game update name to the numeric ID used in entry.version.
[*][B]GetDataVersionKeys()[/B]: update ID to its canonical name. LATEST resolves to the actual update name.
[*][B]GetFurnitureCategories()[/B]: category ID to localised name, parent category and display order.
[/LIST]

If you have to persist keys, use source and update [B]keys[/B], not their numeric values, which can change between releases. GetSourceDetails tells you which acquisition types apply to an item.

[COLOR=wheat][SIZE=3]Coming from old calls[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*]FurC.Find -> LFC.GetEntry. A miss is now nil instead of an empty table.
[*]FurC.GetItemId / FurC.GetItemLink -> LFC.GetItemId / LFC.GetItemLink.
[*]FurC.GetIngredients / FurC.GetMats -> LFC.GetIngredients. Format the returned quantities yourself.
[*]GetSources -> GetSourceDetails. Cost is one table or nil.
[*]SourceType -> GetSourceTypes. Use entry.sources to check membership.
[*]entry.origin -> inspect the first GetSourceDetails record, after checking the list is not empty.
[*]record.source.location / place -> record.source.locations. A list of placements.
[*]record.availability -> entry.version for the update, record.lastSeen for a luxury date.
[/LIST]
